# FinnOS base image
#
# The base is Arch Linux: FinnOS ships its own display server and shell, and
# everything else — the init system, the toolchain, the network stack — is
# the distribution's. What is *not* here is as important as what is: no
# X11, no Wayland, no GTK, no Qt, no XWayland. A machine running FinnOS has
# no display server but the one it was built with.
#
# The two targets:
#
#   ARM64   the dev VM, on Apple Silicon under Parallels
#   X86_64  the release target: an i3-4130 with HD Graphics and 4 GB
#
# The compositor needs the DRM headers, GBM, EGL and FreeType; the GPU
# stack differs between the two.

BASE=base linux linux-firmware systemd networkmanager sudo openssh
AUDIO=alsa-lib alsa-utils alsa-ucm-conf
GRAPHICS_ARM=mesa gbm egl libdrm libinput seatd
GRAPHICS_X86=mesa vulkan-intel intel-ucode libdrm libinput seatd
FONTS=ttf-dejavu ttf-liberation
TOOLS=python python-pip git tar
BUILD=base-devel pkgconf
